1 POST_INSTALL
=prompt Post-installation tasks for PHP for OpenVMS (vms-php)
    VMSPHP$ROOT and USE_ZEND_ALLOC "1" are defined now (system logicals).
    VMSPHP$ROOT is an executive-mode name: an earlier DEFINE/SYSTEM of it
    (supervisor mode) hides it. Remove that one (DEASSIGN/SYSTEM VMSPHP$ROOT)
    and its DEFINE in the startup procedures.
    At boot, add to SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM (after TCP/IP and SSL3):
    $ @SYS$STARTUP:VMSPHP$STARTUP.COM
    DCL symbols php and php_cgi, from LOGIN.COM or SYLOGIN.COM:
    $ @VMSPHP$ROOT:[COM]VMSPHP$SETUP
    The CLI reads VMSPHP$ROOT:[ETC]PHP.INI. A FastCGI pool for lighttpd or Apache
    starts from VMSPHP$ROOT:[ETC]PHP-POOL.INI-DIST (README.VMS).

    USE_ZEND_ALLOC "1" replaces a system "0": VSI's PHP 8.1 needs "0" and crashes
    with "1", so do not run both PHPs on one system.

PRODUCT REMOVE VMSPHP deassigns VMSPHP$ROOT and USE_ZEND_ALLOC; the site's
[ETC]PHP.INI is kept.
